# annotation-of reads FnAnnotation.extra from an annotated function
# Uses plain string-valued fields to avoid ambiguity in return: annotation representation.
# After T-1049 (FnAnnotation.extra) + T-1051 (annotation-of Rust builtin), annotation-of
# returns the extra dict directly. The `doc:` field goes through FnAnnotation.doc (a dedicated
# STANDARD_ANN_KEY path); non-standard fields (like `version:`) go through FnAnnotation.extra.
[f: [fn@[doc: "adds one"  version: "1.0"] [let x@Int] [+ x 1]]]
[ann: [annotation-of f]]
[result-doc: [= ann.doc "adds one"]
 result-ver: [= ann.version "1.0"]]
=== out
Dict({"result-doc": Bool(true), "result-ver": Bool(true)})

=== warn
[NotARecord] expected record type, got Top
[NotARecord] expected record type, got Top
